WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:02.834
-Congrats on everything.
I want to get into everything.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.000
"Funny Girl."
-Okay, let's go.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.601
-I want to get into everything,
but first,

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.467
this is such a cool story,
from what I heard.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.701
The last time you were hear,
it was with Jonathan Groff.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.367
-Right.
-And you sang a song.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:13.634
-Yep.
-Thank you so much for that.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.200
-I appreciate it always,
seeing you.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.801
Through the years,
you've been great to us.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:20.434
-Thank you. No, I was here
in 2019, December, 2019.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.601
And I wanted to tell you,
it was so funny, 'cause

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.234
I was singing a song from
my Christmas album

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:26.667
and we were
in the middle of this

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:29.133
little press tour run
that I was doing.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.100
And I turned to Jonathan
and I was like,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.334
"I really don't know if I can go
on to perform at 'Jimmy.'"

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.801
I was like, "I don't feel good."

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.968
We were walking to the stage
and the floor kept feeling like

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.033
it was coming out from
underneath my feet.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.234
And we did, like -- he's like,

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:43.567
"You're probably just nervous."

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.200
We did a little champagne toast.
We went out that night.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.334
We had so much fun, and
I woke up the next morning

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:51.334
and I said to my husband, I was
like, "I feel so hungover."

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.901
And he was like,
"You didn't drink."

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.701
I was like, "I know.
I just don't feel good."

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:56.834
And he was like, "Do you think
you might be pregnant?"

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.434
I was like, "No!"

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.734
It didn't really seem like
it was in the cards for us.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.300
I was like, "No, there can't --"

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.501
He was like,
"You should just check."

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.000
And I was! Here!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
At the show!

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.100
-On our show?
-Yeah!

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.634
-You were pregnant on our show!
-I was, and I had no idea.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:13.968
-And how old is he?

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.400
-He's 2.
He just turned 2 in August.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.701
-I have to say hi. Hi, Ever.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.667
Mommy's at work.
I love you so much.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:23.968
-Oh, my God. That's amazing.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.667
-Yeah. It's been wild.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.000
-Does he love
when you sing to him?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.968
-That's a fun question. Yeah.
-Okay, alright.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.901
Sorry. He doesn't?
-No, I mean --

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:35.000
So this is the first time
I've gone back to work.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.601
I've been home with him
for the past two years 100%,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:39.934
and now I'm back to work.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:41.434
So my singing coach was like,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.501
you know, try to incorporate
what you're doing,

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.567
like, try to incorporate him
into it

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:46.901
so he can be a part of it

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.267
and you can be not away
from him as much.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.834
So I was warming up
the other day

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.567
and my husband was like,
"Should we come in?"

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:55.200
I was like, "Yes, come in.
Watch me do my warm up."

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.267
And I hit some high note,

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:00.200
and he started
hysterically crying.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:02.501
Disaster?
-I'm like, okay.

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.100
That was a big fail.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.701
-That one's not gonna work.
Well, we tried.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.868
-I tell him all the time,
I'm like,

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.767
"What do you want
to hear tonight? Anything.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.200
Do you want Celine?
Do you want Barbara?"

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.267
-Taking requests!
-Anything you want.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.701
"Baba? Baba Greengrass."

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:19.200
And I don't know if you've heard
"The Green Grass Grows,"

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.701
but that one is just...

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.033
It's a real
tough one for parents.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.767
It's just the same thing
over and over.

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:25.934
-Oh, no, no, no.

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:29.567
I'm over that phase
of those songs.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.334
I mean,
if I heard the Backpack song

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:32.634
one more time, from Dora,
I was going to...

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.400
-Oh, no, no.
-...find the person

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.467
and murder them.

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.934
I know they're bringing joy
to people, but I had enough.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.601
-I wake up in the morning...
-It would haunt me, yeah.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:43.701
-The first thing I hear is,
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.067
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.901
-♪ Peppa Pig ♪ -- Yeah.
-Over and over again.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.667
-I know every single theme song.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.834
-I know every song
on "Daniel Tiger."

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.100
Like, I know it all.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.534
-Yeah, yeah, I loved it,

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:57.133
and I'm so happy
I'm done with that phase.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.534
-Well, we are
in the thick of it.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:02:59.934
-You are in the thick of it.
-We are in the thick of it.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.200
-Get ready.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.267
Can I just read you
some nice reviews here?

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.367
-Oh, my goodness.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:05.801
-For your performance
in "Funny Girl."

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:09.300
"Lea Michele is a revelation
as Fanny Brice," says 'The Cut.'

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.000
"Lea Michele is stupendous.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.834
'Funny Girl' has a missile,

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.801
a performer who,
from her first words,

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:15.968
'Hello, gorgeous,'

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.901
shoots straight
to her target and hits it.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.234
"The New York Times" said that.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:22.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:25.100
How about this?
"The Washington Post" said,

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.133
"Lea Michele doesn't just
bring down the house,

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.534
she brings down
the whole darn block."

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:30.801
"Washington Post."

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.033
That's how you do it!
That's how you do it.

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.634
And my friend went to go
see you opening night,

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.834
and I want to six or seven

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.901
standing ovations
during the play,

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:45.067
during the song,
mid-song standing ovations.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.367
Buddy, you hit a home
run on this.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:49.000
-Thank you. It's been so
awesome. It's been great.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.801
-How does it feel
to be back on Broadway?

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.934
-Oh, my God,
that in and of itself

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.834
is just so unbelievable.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.133
I'd been wanting to come back
to Broadway for so many years.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:03:59.801
I was gone for 15 years.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.501
"Spring Awakening"
was the last show that I did.

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:02.534
[ Light applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:04.133
-But to be back... Yay!

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:07.033
To be back
and to be in the show

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.300
that I've loved
for so many years.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.701
But I'm such a fan
of this production.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.701
Incredible cast,
this incredible score.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:17.501
-Can we even just talk about
the "Glee" of it all?

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.501
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.767
-I'm getting goosebumps.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:24.434
I loved you, obviously,
on "Glee."

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.434
We've done bits since then.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.868
You've always been great.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:32.267
I've watched probably 100 times,
you sing "Rain on my Parade."

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:33.801
and I would cry.

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.334
I'd go show everyone,

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.067
"You want to see the best thing
you've ever seen on television?"

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.801
Watch Lea Michele sing this.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:42.033
Oh my gosh, now you're
doing it on Broadway.

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.467
-Now I'm doing it!
-It is like...

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:46.467
-I know, it's really awesome.
It's so fantastic.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:49.667
I mean, but, you know,
look, I'm 36 now,

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:52.501
and the story of
"Funny Girl" spans

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.767
through the course of,
you know, many years.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:59.434
You see her love
and her loss and her failures

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.567
and her successes
and becoming a mom and a wife.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.067
And I feel like at this point,
being where I am right now,

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:05.234
it's just perfect.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.601
Timing is everything,
and I'm so grateful.

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:09.367
-It couldn't
happen to a better person.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.801
-Thank you so much.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:13.067
-We love you,
and you're performing for us.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I am.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.634
-Lea Michele
is performing for us.

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:19.901
Check out "Funny Girl"
on Broadway.com for tickets.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:22.100
Lea is performing a song from
"Funny Girl" when we come back.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.133
Stick around!

